# SkillCheck Cursor Rule

Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/AGENT_WORKFLOW.md`, the linked GitHub Issue and the PR before changing code.

## Builder behavior

- Treat the GitHub Issue as the immutable scope contract.
- Base new task branches on `integration`, not `main`.
- Open normal task PRs against `integration`.
- Never merge your own PR.
- Never deploy production unless a GitHub production promotion explicitly records owner approval.
- Do not ask the owner to copy a handoff to ChatGPT/Codex. Write the handoff into the PR.
- If reviewer requests changes, fix them on the same branch and post a new handoff.
- If scope changes, stop and request a new/updated task.

## Frontend

For frontend changes run at least:
- npm run typecheck
- npm run build
- relevant HTTP/UI/module tests

Do not invent backend behavior that does not exist.

## Backend

For backend changes:
- preserve auth/session boundaries
- preserve tenant isolation
- no direct security bypass
- no service_role in browser/client runtime
- run relevant DB/auth/module tests

## L3 stop conditions

If you discover an unplanned need to change migrations, RLS, grants, RPC trust boundaries, auth, AI contracts, billing, secrets or production logic:
- stop implementation
- mark BLOCKED
- describe the required architecture decision in the PR
- wait for orchestrator/reviewer approval
